## Claim
Text: "President Ferdinand Marcos and Dr. Jose Rizal established and founded the WORLD BANK and International Monetary Fund."
Claim author: Bangon Bansang Maharlika
Claim date: October 22, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### What are the historically recognized founding dates and locations for the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund (IMF)?
Answer: The World Bank opened its doors for business on June 25, 1946, at its headquarters at 1818 H Street in Washington, D.C., while the International Monetary Fund (IMF) held its founding Boards of Governors meeting in Savannah, Georgia, from March 1–18, 1946.

Source URL: https://pubdocs.worldbank.org/en/683991541019930363/70-years-chapter-one.pdf

### Which international agreement or conference officially established the World Bank and the IMF?
Answer: The World Bank and the International Monetary Fund (IMF) were officially established by the **Bretton Woods Agreement**, which was negotiated in July 1944 at the United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference held in Bretton Woods, New Hampshire. As the source states, "The Bretton Woods Agreement also created two important organizations—the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and the World Bank."

Source URL: https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/brettonwoodsagreement.asp

### Was President Ferdinand Marcos of the Philippines a signatory or delegate to the agreement that established the World Bank and the IMF?
Answer: Based on the provided search result, there is no evidence that President Ferdinand Marcos of the Philippines was a signatory or delegate to the Bretton Woods Agreement. The source details the conference's key figures and structure, noting the commissions were chaired by Harry Dexter White (U.S.), John Maynard Keynes (U.K.), and Eduardo Suárez (Mexico), but it does not list Marcos among the delegates. The conference took place in 1944, before Marcos's presidency began in 1965, making his participation historically implausible.

Source URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bretton_Woods_Conference

### Was Dr. Jose Rizal, the Philippine national hero who was executed in 1896, alive during the period when the World Bank and IMF were established?
Answer: Dr. Jose Rizal was executed in 1896, more than four decades before the World Bank and International Monetary Fund were established at the Bretton Woods Conference in 1944.

Source URL: https://tagacalamba.wixsite.com/calamba/single-post/2016/06/19/rizal-lived-to-be-113-did-not-die-in-bagumbayan

### What was the documented role of the Philippines or its representatives in the founding conferences of the World Bank and IMF?
Answer: Based on the search result, the Philippines or its representatives had no documented role in the founding conferences of the World Bank and IMF. The source states that the United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference at Bretton Woods involved "delegates from 44 Allied and socialist countries," with leadership from the United States and the United Kingdom, and does not mention the Philippines or any Filipino representatives in a founding capacity.

Source URL: https://www.nhpr.org/the-exchange/2019-07-08/75-years-ago-n-h-s-bretton-woods-conference-reshaped-world-economic-policy

### Is there any historical record, treaty, or official document from the World Bank or IMF that names Ferdinand Marcos as a founder?
Answer: Based on the search result, there is no historical record, treaty, or official document from the World Bank that names Ferdinand Marcos as a founder. The source explicitly states that "The World Bank was established in 1944 to help rebuild Europe and Japan after World War II," and its largest founding shareholders were countries like the United States, Japan, Germany, the United Kingdom, and France. No mention is made of the Philippines or Ferdinand Marcos in a founding capacity.

Source URL: https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/feature/2012/07/26/getting_to_know_theworldbank

