### What is the source or origin of the claim that Ferdinand Marcos and Jose Rizal founded the World Bank and IMF, and what evidence does that source provide?
Answer: The claim originates from a segment script titled "dctvteleprompt4-4-17" on a platform discussing the "Global Currency Reset" (GCR), which asserts that José Rizal and Ferdinand Marcos created the World Bank and IMF to facilitate a planned transition of global assets. However, the source provides no verifiable historical evidence beyond stating this as part of a belief system within the GCR narrative, emphasizing instead that "enough people now believe" in the legitimacy of this account.

Source URL: https://www.scribd.com/document/429131830/dctvteleprompt4-4-17

## Final Judgement
Based on the recorded evidence, the key findings conclusively refute the claim. The World Bank and IMF were established at the Bretton Woods Conference in 1944, with no documented involvement of the Philippines or its representatives. Dr. Jose Rizal was executed in 1896, over four decades before these institutions were founded. Ferdinand Marcos was not president until 1965 and there is no evidence he was a delegate to the 1944 conference. The claim's origin is traced to a non-credible source promoting an alternative narrative without historical support.

No further information is required as the evidence clearly and directly contradicts the claim on all points: the timing, the individuals involved, and the documented founding process.

The historical record explicitly refutes the claim that Ferdinand Marcos and Jose Rizal founded the World Bank and IMF. The institutions were created by international agreement in 1944, and neither individual was involved in their establishment. `refuted`

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted. Historical records confirm that the [World Bank](https://pubdocs.worldbank.org/en/683991541019930363/70-years-chapter-one.pdf) and [IMF](https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/brettonwoodsagreement.asp) were established by international agreement at the [Bretton Woods Conference in 1944](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bretton_Woods_Conference). Dr. Jose Rizal was executed in 1896, over four decades before this conference. Ferdinand Marcos was not a delegate to the 1944 conference and there is no historical record of his involvement in the institutions' founding, with [World Bank sources](https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/feature/2012/07/26/getting_to_know_theworldbank) omitting him entirely. The claim's origin is a [non-credible source](https://www.scribd.com/document/429131830/dctvteleprompt4-4-17) promoting an alternative narrative without historical support.